ept instead, which would make both the bal write and the 9+4N sizing vestigial. Observation path and completion: write, sync, close, read back, then emit, with no wait, join or cleanup duty.\\n\\nLimits kept explicit: no reader of the stable store exists in the snapshot, so the intended offsets are inferred from the recorder's own writes and buffer size; the shipped run.go passes durable=false, so this is an implementation-semantics defect rather than a live failure in the default deployment; and only one instance and record are observed, leaving repeated records, the Deps region and partial writes uncompared. No map object, requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened.\"}"}}
